# Docker build-context ignore rules.
# OWNER: deployment contract (ARCHITECTURE.md §1). Docker resolves .dockerignore ONLY from the
# build-context root (repo root) or as `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile — never
# from a plain deployment/.dockerignore — so this file lives here, while deployment/Dockerfile
# remains the image recipe owner. One owner per responsibility; no second ignore file.

# VCS / editor
.git
.vscode
.idea

# Dependencies / build output (image builds its own)
node_modules
dist
build
.vite
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — never enter the image context; .env.example (placeholders only) is kept on purpose
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test + tooling artifacts (not needed by `npm run build` or runtime)
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
tests
e2e
tmp
.tmp
scratch
logs
*.log

# Docs / spec — not needed to build or run the image
docs
ProjectSpec
*.md
